From 1e578eac6158c5d7884e1603ee7fa6a97748d7c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 21:26:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 462/468] AOSCOS: PCI: Use local_pci_probe() when the elected
 CPU is offline

The queue_work_on() based pci_call_probe() elects a target CPU from
cpumask_of_node(node) intersected with
housekeeping_cpumask(HK_TYPE_DOMAIN) without considering whether that
CPU is online.  With a node online while all its CPUs are offline
(e.g. "maxcpus=1" without "nr_cpus=1"), the elected CPU can be
offline (possibly never onlined); the probe work is then queued to a
per-cpu worker pool that has no workers and can never gain one, so
flush_work() blocks forever.

Extend the cpu < nr_cpu_ids gate with cpu_online(cpu) so that such a
probe falls back to calling local_pci_probe() directly, reusing the
existing no-suitable-CPU fallback path.  The test sits inside the same
RCU read-side section as the election and the enqueue, and hotplug is
disabled via cpu_hotplug_disable(), so the decision cannot be raced
by a concurrent CPU hotplug operation.

Adapted from the work_on_cpu()-based fix by Huacai Chen and Hongchen
Zhang (lore: 20250511083413.3326421-2-chenhuacai@loongson.cn), which
no longer applies after upstream's rewrite of pci_call_probe() to the
queue_work_on() + flush_work() structure.

This commit was not runtime-tested (no reproducer environment was
available); a defconfig build of drivers/pci/pci-driver.o completed
with no warnings.

